 "brief": "A riser that lifts one leg of a bed by 50 mm, PLA on FDM, printed standing up (layers along Z). It stands on a wooden floor (the plane z = 0) and stays inside x = -40 to 40, y = -40 to 40, z = 0 to 60. The bed's 50 x 50 mm square leg sits in a socket in its top: the socket is 51 x 51 mm, 10 mm deep (its floor at z = 50), open at the top, corners rounded 2 mm. Each leg carries a quarter of 300 kg (bed, mattress, two people), and 2 g when someone drops onto the bed; with the plain weight on it, a 150 N shove sideways (along X or along Y) when the bed is pushed. Nothing screws it down: it stays put by friction on the floor (about 0.3). Safety factor 2.",
